[[63,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Remove the protective cap (1a), and using an ordinary punch, unscrew the shear bolt (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223003103.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[63,7,0,"<p>1. Undo the bolt (1a) and remove the handle (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223003104.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[63,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Fit the handle (1a) in its seating and tighten the bolt (1b).</p><p>2. Use a new shear bolt and tighten until the head breaks.</p><p>3. Fit the protective cap.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223003105.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]]